/PATTERN LIBRARY - KINSTON
/%RC	SHORTHAND CODE DEFINITIONS

/   	USE OF THE SYMBOLS DEFINED BELOW PERMITS
/	THE DESCRIPTION OF ANY SPINNERET PATTERN
/	IN SHORTHAND FORM. UPON ASSEMBLY, THESE SYMBOLS
/	ARE GIVEN THEIR NUMERICAL EQUIVALENTS,WHICH THE
/	ASP PROGRAMS DECODE AND PROPERLY EXECUTE DURING
/	PROGRAM OPERATION.

	OCTAL

	PATNUM=0    /SEQUENTIAL PATTERN NUMBER
	RECTAN=0    /RECTANGULAR PATTERN CODE
	POLAR=1     /POLAR PATTERN CODE
	H=4000      /HEADER: BIT 0 = 1
	PX=2000     /+ X OFFSET: BIT 1 = 1
	MX=1000     /- X OFFSET: BIT 2 = 1
	PY=400      /+ Y OFFSET: BIT 3 = 1
	MY=200      /- Y OFFSET: BIT 4 = 1
	PXR=100     /+ X REPEAT: BIT 5 = 1
	MXR=0000    /- X REPEAT: BIT 5 = 0
	PA=2000     /+ ANGULAR OFFSET: BIT 1 = 1
	MA=0000     /- ANGULAR OFFSET: BIT 1 = 0
	ARC=1000    /ARC VALUE: BIT 2 = 1
	BEGIN=4000  /PATTERN INITIATOR CODE
	OVER=4000   /PATTERN TERMINATOR CODE


	FIELD 1
	*1265
	DECIMAL




/%RC	SPINNERET PATTERN LIBRARY


/   	THE TABLE BELOW IS THE STORAGE FOR THE ACTUAL
/	SPINNERET PATTERNS ENCODED IN THE ASP SYSTEM
/	TO POSITION THESE SPINNERETS FOR INSPECTION.
/	THIS TABLE MAY BE ADDED TO OR DELETED FROM AS
/	NECESSARY. FOR AN EXPLANATION OF THE SHORT-
/	HAND, WITH EXAMPLES, SEE THE BEGINNING OF
/	THE MEMORY FIELD OR SEE THE ASP MANUAL.
/	FOR PATTERN UPDATING PROCEDURES REFER TO THE ASP
/	MANUAL.






